30,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My research shows a problem. Some bikes are exposed to rain, and people are already shifting other machines just to leave in the morning.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The building account is nearly empty for capital work. Also, the ward park is expensive and has a long waiting list, making it a poor alternative.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,George,,"It seems the same flats have held the covered spots for years without review. Interestingly, daily riders said they'd prefer paying over equal claims.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"I found that charging for spaces in a nearby block caused arrears and social withdrawal. However, our own complaint log shows vague frustrations with leaning bikes.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh no! The treasurer already spends hours on small collections, and those fancy display frames are actually hard to use and need maintenance!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@George, if the same people have had the best spots for years, that explains the tension. The physical layout is definitely contributing to the friction.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, if the treasurer is already burdened, adding a complex billing system for every single space might be impractical.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,George,,"@Asuka, you are right. The lack of review is a problem. But the fact that frequent users are willing to pay is a useful data point.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, the financial side is risky. If we implement a paid system, we might end up with neighbors who stop speaking to us entirely.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, if it's a shoving match in the morning, we definitely need a better way to organize the bikes!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"We need a solution that addresses the ""best"" and ""worst"" spots. A simple lottery or open access might not solve the rain or congestion issues.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,We must balance the need for funds with the administrative burden Mio mentioned. A system that is too complex will just fail.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,George,,I believe we should consider the preferences of the daily riders. They are the ones most affected by the current chaos.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I agree with Ryuji. Whatever we do, it must not destroy the social fabric of the lobby. A rigid system can be very cold.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Mio,,I just don't want one person to end up doing all the paperwork! Let's keep it simple so everyone stays happy!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
