55,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option B's double-tier racks sound efficient, but Mio's finding about the display frames suggests they are a physical hassle. I prefer Option C.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A provides income, but the administrative burden and the risk of arrears Shunichi mentioned make me hesitate. Option C is cleaner.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,George,,"Option A aligns with what the daily riders suggested. However, Option C ensures that the ""best"" spots aren't held by the same people forever.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is a social disaster waiting to happen. Option B is too chaotic. Option C is the most neutral way to handle the scarcity.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option B sounds like a lot of work to maintain those frames! Option A is too much paperwork for the treasurer. I vote for Option C!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, I agree. Option C is the most logical way to distribute the burden of the rain-exposed spots fairly over time.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, if we avoid the payment system, we avoid the arrears. Option C is the most stable choice for the building's harmony.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, I see your point. While I liked the idea of payment, a yearly draw is a fair way to reset the status quo.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, exactly. A lottery is a ""act of god"" that no one can personally resent. It keeps the peace in the lobby.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Mio,,Yay! Option C is like a little surprise every year! It's fair and doesn't make anyone do too much work!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I vote for Option C. It is the only way to ensure the physical disparities of the parking rows are shared equitably.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for Option C. It avoids financial conflict and administrative overload while solving the allocation problem.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,George,,I vote for Option C. It corrects the long-term stagnation of the current arrangement in a way everyone can accept.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for Option C. It is the most rational choice to prevent social friction and avoid the pitfalls of a paid system.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Mio,,I vote for Option C! It's the happiest and easiest way for everyone!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
